  },
  {
   "id": "a25-text-60",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1125,
   "y": 790,
   "width": 496,
   "height": 170,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 475140,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 6283740,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "•  Empty list: the outgoing interface is enough (the\n   LFA case). Example 1, S → D: \"no SIDs needed\".\n•  Flex-Algo (A24): each algorithm has its own\n   locator (RFC 9350 §14).\n•  An End.X SID needs no node SID before it (RFC\n   9855 §7.2): that could save a SID; not modelled.\n•  The packet walk (A7) and the simulation’s labels\n   stay SR-MPLS.",
   "originalText": "•  Empty list: the outgoing interface is enough (the\n   LFA case). Example 1, S → D: \"no SIDs needed\".\n•  Flex-Algo (A24): each algorithm has its own\n   locator (RFC 9350 §14).\n•  An End.X SID needs no node SID before it (RFC\n   9855 §7.2): that could save a SID; not modelled.\n•  The packet walk (A7) and the simulation’s labels\n   stay SR-MPLS.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
